      "text": "The median of a set is the middle number when the numbers are arranged in ascending order. Given that the median is 9, we know that when the set $\\{n, n + 5, n + 6, n + 9, n + 15\\}$ is arranged in ascending order, the middle number, which is the median, is $n + 6$. Therefore, we have:\n\\[ n + 6 = 9 \\]\nSolving for $n$, we subtract 6 from both sides:\n\\[ n = 9 - 6 \\]\n\\[ n = 3 \\]\nNow that we have the value of $n$, we can find the mean of the set. The set is $\\{3, 8, 9, 12, 18\\}$. The mean is the sum of the elements divided by the number of elements. The sum of the elements is:\n\\[ 3 + 8 + 9 + 12 + 18 = 50 \\]\nThe number of elements is 5. Therefore, the mean is:\n\\[ \\text{Mean} = \\frac{50}{5} = 10 \\]\nSo, the mean of the set is:\n\\[ \\boxed{10} \\]",
